{
  "name": "merge-node-ids",
  "description": "S2f. Literal ids that address the sub-page's own nodes get the prefix: the `animationId` prop, `animationId` of a tween or tweenSequence Value and of animateForward and animateReverse, `dialogId`, `id` of updateComponent and deleteComponent, `subPageId` of updateSubPage. A Value in one of those fields is not an id: only the page-state key inside it is rewritten. A nested SubPage node is a node like any other: its id gets the prefix, which is how its own prefix composes later. The Hero `tag`, a navigate route, a tab id, `pageId` and `mode` are left alone. A node id and a state key may be the same string: the id is rewritten where an id goes and the key where a key goes, and a plain string (a Text's `data`, an updateComponent's `data`) stays.",
  "kind": "merge",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "animation, dialog, mutation and sub-page ids",
      "prefix": "detail:",
